.TH HOSTNAME "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
hostname \- set or print the name of the current host system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hostname
[\fI\,NAME\/\fR]
.br
.B hostname
\fI\,OPTION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Print or set the hostname of the current system.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/hostname#hostname--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/hostname#hostname--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
